Compile out MFC functions that call what WinSCP's MFC subset never builds.

CObject::IsKindOf and the two down-cast helpers call
CRuntimeClass::IsDerivedFrom, which upstream already excludes under WINSCP;
timecore.cpp's CArchive stream operators call CArchive members whose
arccore.cpp is not vendored. Nothing in WinSCP uses any of them, and
C++Builder's linker never complained, but lld resolves every reference in an
object it pulls in. They join upstream's own #ifndef WINSCP exclusions, on
lines that were blank, so line counts are unchanged.

--- a/libs/mfc/source/objcore.cpp	2026-10-11 13:36:53.811476579 -0300
+++ b/libs/mfc/source/objcore.cpp	2026-10-11 13:36:53.818287396 -0300
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
 {
 	return RUNTIME_CLASS(CObject);
 }
-
+#ifndef WINSCP
 BOOL CObject::IsKindOf(const CRuntimeClass* pClass) const
 {
 	ASSERT(this != NULL);
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@
 	return pObject;
 }
 #endif
-
+#endif
 /////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 // Diagnostic Support
 
